4. No stray files; temporary work cleaned or archived with a manifest row.

## Delegating to another agent

If you are a coordinator handing work to a delegate, insert a preamble into
the PREAMBLE SLOT at the top of the delegate's view of this file, carrying
anything the delegate must know that this committed file cannot. Examples:

- Subagent policy: "do not spawn subagents" / "use a workflow" /
  "decompose recursively into the smallest verifiable units"
- Budget: max steps, tokens, time, or spend for this run
- Scope: exact files/paths in bounds; everything else read-only
- Forbidden actions this run (no commits, no installs, no network, …)
- Report-back format and where evidence must land

Rules: the preamble may narrow authority and scope, never widen them; it
never contradicts Hard constraints above (constraints win); it is
run-specific and never committed.
